---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand } from '../data/site';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', item: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', item: '/privacy/' }];
const updated = 'September 12, 2026';
---
<Base title={`Privacy | ${brand.name}`} description={`What the ${brand.name} quote and lead forms collect, where your details are kept, who sees them, and how to ask us to delete them.`} crumbs={crumbs}>
  <section class="sec"><div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What happens to your details</h1>
    <p>You give us your name and number so we can call you about your turf. Here is what the forms on this site collect and where it goes.</p>
    <h2>What the forms collect</h2>
    <p>The quote form asks for your name, phone number, ZIP code, what you need, and optionally your email and a message. The follow-up form for people who reached us through a Facebook ad asks about turf size, pets, the problem, the best time to call, and your first name and phone. Each submission also records the page it was sent from.</p>
    <h2>What we use it for</h2>
    <p>To call, text or email you about your quote and your turf. We do not sell or share your details with anyone else, and we do not add you to a mailing list.</p>
    <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
    <p>The forms are handled by Netlify, the company that hosts this site, which stores each submission for us. If you reached us through a Facebook lead form, Meta also holds the details you entered there under its own policy.</p>
    <h2>Other services this site uses</h2>
    <p>Fonts load from Google Fonts. Pages that came from a Facebook ad may carry the Meta Pixel so we can see whether the ad worked; it does not see what you type into our forms. This site runs no other analytics or advertising trackers.</p>
    <h2>Deleting your details</h2>
    <p>Ask and we will delete your submission: call <a href={brand.phoneHref}>{brand.phone}</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.</p>
    <p class="src">Last updated {updated}.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
